the new palace is the biggest castle  ever built for King Frederick the Great  yet  it is greatly unknown noir stories tend  to flock to his private residence  sanssouci on the other side of the park  so we decided to take a closer look at  the new palace Frederick the Great had  the Baroque Palace built at the end of  the Seven Years War  construction work took place from 1763  to 1769 and just six and a half years he  sought to demonstrate the power and  glories of Prussia calling the building  and from fava nut which is a synonym for  boastful this was also the goal of this  palace to show that the Prussians were  still a great power the king himself  rarely spent time in the new palace it  was predominantly used to accommodate  his guests  [Music]  the grotto hall is impressive displaying  over 20,000 and crusted shouts and  stones another exceptional feature is a  marble floor it was inspired by the  seabed  [Music]  directly above the grotto hole is this  fantastic marble hole it measures 600  square meters and it is 16 meters high  it is a miracle that it hasn't collapsed  yet as it is free-floating supported  only by wooden beams  that's why visitors like me can just  walk over these glass walkways  [Music]  noble men and women used to dine in the  banquet hall it still has the original  wallpaper which is 250 years old  usually guests in a palace were given  two rooms but the new palace was so big  that everyone was allocated ten rooms to  use and each room is as large as an  average families house  [Music]  this is the back of the new palace this  place was used for events like big  festivals and military ceremonies  when you visit pot stop don't just go to  salsa si make sure that you include the  new palace in your agenda it is very  worth a trip
 

